 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** Rendering performance is competitive with hardware-accelerated 3D texture sampling [S2].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Significant memory savings compared to dense textures [S2]. For the Galaxy dataset (108 GB raw), VDB achieves 14 GB at 1:8 rate [S1]. NanoVDB overhead is ~10% for large datasets [S2].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Significant memory savings compared to dense textures [S2]. NanoVDB overhead is ~10% for large datasets [S2].
 *   **Measured Performance:**
     *   Galaxy dataset: VDB achieves 34.8 FPS on 1 GPU vs 18.6 FPS for dense textures on 3 GPUs [S1].
